    "controls": "y",
    "capability_check": "y",
    "uncertainty_reported": "y",
    "code_released": "not stated",
    "peer_reviewed": "Proceedings of the 34th ACM International Conference on Multimedia (MM ’26)",
    "problems": "The intervention is an opaque, indivisible post-condition, so its method and components cannot be attributed. Findings use a fixed CLIP judge and are operational frequencies rather than human-reference oracle measures; the paper cautions that judge error may vary by configuration. The reported residual/bypass values do not have stated confidence intervals in Table 2, and the study does not establish chance-level performance or general capability retention.",
    "rows_left_out": "Omitted non-intervention model/channel results not paired with the post-condition, and calibration/action-sensitivity results unrelated to the claim's recovery mechanisms. The relevant post-condition residual and bypass entries from Table 2 and their described aggregate values are included.",
    "untested": [],
    "missing": [],
    "verdict_notes": "The reader's T3/tests guess is rejected. The study's system (diffusion models) and its intervention (an opaque, unnamed condition) do not match what the versions name. Even read loosely as version E, standard-attack bypass is lower than the matched residual, and only obfuscation exceeds it. Bypass rows also wrongly omit the residual as their baseline."
